    "reason": "The first deployment used anchor1/anchor2/anchor3 addresses derived from the well-known Anvil/Hardhat default mnemonic ('test test test ... junk'). Live chain data caught the problem before any real scenario data was written: funding those addresses with 0.01 ETH each was immediately followed by balance 0 and nonzero nonces (8 and 10 on the first two indices) from an unrelated sender — standing bots drain any funds sent to those addresses on public testnets because the keys are public knowledge. scripts/identities.mjs was changed to derive keys from a project-specific non-secret seed instead (keccak256-based, not BIP-39), and the whole stack (anchor book + all six contracts) was redeployed clean. The abandoned first GenesisAnchorBook was at 0x824C1D3126a25365182e194277D3749D7a1bC34e and the abandoned AvalToken/AvalRegistry/CredibilityVault/PlatformRegistry/ReportRegistry/PresenceDrip set began at deploy tx 0xa0e20b32b11741143421e68f0c7e0c5fed22f26f05e93f755306ff157922d480 (block 32216062) — both orphaned, no enroll/vouch data was ever written to them (only one enroll() call was attempted against the old registry and it reverted before any state changed)."
  },
